      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This distinction touches upon deep debates in art history regarding Western and non-Western canons. While mainstream Western discourse often privileges the singular genius pursuing abstract truth, viewing non-Western art solely through \"function\" risks flattening its aesthetic power. A balanced approach treats the Renaissance piece as a pursuit of universal humanism, while framing the West African objects as embodying a rich, localized cosmological system. Their \"value\" lies in their successful negotiation between artistic form and essential ritual purpose.",
